RAMSES parameter file for the DustySlab test -- VARIANT B (IR-trapping regime).

Uniform static isothermal gas with a dust slab at 3-7 pc. UV is injected at the
left edge, streams freely through the dust-poor gas, and is absorbed inside the
slab and reprocessed into the IR.

Expected behaviour:
  1. x < 3 pc : UV streams freely (eps=1e-6), dust acceleration = kappa_rp*F_UV/c
  2. x > 3 pc : UV attenuated, tau_UV(slab) = 4.5, so the direct acceleration
                falls by ~e^-4.5 across the slab
  3. IR appears where the UV is absorbed, giving an IR energy peak in the slab.
     In THIS variant the cell-crossing IR optical depth is
     tau_cell = 1.5*dx*kappa_R*rho_d ~ 8e-6, so f_trap = exp(-2/3tau_c) = 0 and
     the IR stays entirely in the STREAMING band -- there is no trapped IR.
     Use dustyslab_dense.nml for the trapping regime.

Gas opacity is off by construction: the UV band is 5-7 eV, below every
ionisation threshold tracked by RTZ (Mg 7.65, Fe 7.9, Si 8.15, C 11.26,
H 13.6 eV), so group_csn is identically zero there. Photoionisation is also
switched off in the network.

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
rt=.true.
static=.true.
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=7
levelmax=7
ngridmax=4000
nparttot=1
nexpand=1
boxlen=10.0
/

&BOUNDARY_PARAMS
nboundary=2
ibound_min=-1,+1
ibound_max=-1,+1
bound_type= 2, 2
/

&INIT_PARAMS
condinit_kind='dustyslabthick'
nregion=1
region_type(1)='square'
x_center=5.0
length_x=10.0
d_region=1.23d5           ! = 1.23e-17 g/cm3 -> tau_cell,IR ~ 1 (trapping ON)
u_region=0.0
p_region=8.7857d4         ! same c_s = 1 code unit (isothermal, grad(Pg)=0)
var_region(1,:)=0.0
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
noutput=5
tout = 0.05,0.1,0.2,0.35,0.5
tend = 0.5
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.4
courant_factor=0.8
slope_type=2
riemann='hllc'
data_dir = '/Users/currodri/Documents/RAMSES_dev/rtzdata_for_public_ramses/'
/

&COOLING_PARAMS
metal = .true.
cooling = .false.
/

&REFINE_PARAMS
interpol_var=0
interpol_type=2
/

&UNITS_PARAMS
units_length = 3.08567758149137d18 ! 1 pc in cm
units_density = 1e-22              ! so d_region=1 <=> rho0 = 1e-22 g/cm3
units_time = 3.1556926d13          ! 1 Myr in s
/

&RT_PARAMS
rt_flux_scheme='glf'          ! mandatory for IR trapping (RT15 footnote 3)
rt_c_fraction=0.001           ! c_red = 307 code units >> c_s = 1
rt_otsa=.true.
rt_is_init_xion=.false.
rt_Tconst=115.0d0             ! isothermal, keeps grad(P_gas)=0 and c_s fixed
rt_nsubcycle=500
rt_isIR=.true.                ! group 1 is the IR band
rt_isIRtrap=.true.            ! trapped IR in the NENER slot (inactive here, tau_cell<<1)
!----------- RTZ params -----------!
rtz_cooling=.true.
rtz_include_collisional_ionization=.false.
rtz_include_photoionization=.false.   ! no gas opacity
rtz_include_cosmic_ray_ionization=.false.
rtz_include_charge_exchange=.false.
rtz_include_dust_recombination=.false.
rtz_include_HM12_UVB=.false.
isH2_rtz=.false.
isCO_rtz=.false.
rtz_UV_background_G0=0.d0
rtz_max_cool_timestep=1.d20
!----------- UV inflow at the left edge -----------!
! RAMSES-RT's rt_n_bound injects only into rtvar 1, i.e. group 1, which
! rt_isIR reserves for the IR. So the UV inflow is a thin square source region
! at x=0 targeting group 2, with rt_u_source=1 (fully directed +x). The source
! imposes a fixed photon density each RT subcycle (rt_sources_vsweep), so it
! acts as a steady inflow.
! rt_n_source is a photon NUMBER FLUX [photons/cm2/s]; 1.5e9 gives
! w_d ~ 0.3 c_s in the dust-poor gas, subsonic and under the tva_wmax_cs cap.
rt_nsource = 1
rt_source_type(1) = 'square'
rt_exp_source(1) = 10.0
rt_src_x_center(1) = 0.0
rt_src_length_x(1) = 0.15
rt_u_source(1) = 1.0
rt_n_source(1) = 1.5d9
rt_src_group(1) = 2
/

&RT_GROUPS
! group 1 = IR (far-IR, where ~30 K dust re-emits); group 2 = UV, 5-7 eV,
! deliberately below all tracked ionisation thresholds so the gas is transparent.
group_egy     = 0.01, 6.0
groupL0       = 0.001, 5.0
groupL1       = 0.1,   7.0
/

&CALIMA_PARAMS
dust_tva=.true.
dust_radpressure=.true.
use_w_drift_test=.false.
dust_composition(1,6) = 1d0
dustbins_per_chemtype=1
asize=0.01d0                  ! must match averaged_cross_section_DustBin_01.txt (0.01 um)
sgrain=2.2d0
amin = 3d-3
amax = 3d-2
charging_model='RM2026'
dust_tables_dir='/Users/currodri/Documents/RAMSES_dev/rtzdata_for_public_ramses/calima_data/'
/
